  "notes": "Fetched from ORC's public, unauthenticated certificate feed as JSON and transformed here with no hand editing (the generator is quoted in the phase-05 progress log). Four things differ from the J/70's committed Speed Guide and each is a judgement this file has to state rather than hide.\n\n1. ORC publishes allowances in seconds per nautical mile, not speeds. bsKt = 3600/allowance, which is exact. The Beat and Run allowances are VMG made good, so their boat speed is 3600/allowance divided by cos(BeatAngle) or cos(GybeAngle); vmgKt for those rows is 3600/allowance itself, negative downwind by this schema's sign convention. vmgKt on the fixed-angle rows is bsKt x cos(TWA).\n\n2. The feed does not tag which sail the VPP chose at each fixed angle; the sail-resolved Speed Guide is a paid per-boat product (ADR 0020). The tag here is read off the boat's sail plan, not off the VPP: a Melges 24 carries one headsail and one sprit-tacked asymmetric, so the 52, 60 and 75 degree rows are the jib and the 90 degrees and beyond rows are the kite. 90 degrees is the weakest of those calls -- in the lightest winds the VPP may still be under the jib there -- and it is one of the three angles ADR 0012's hold-out gate scores, so a failure on the TWS 8 or 14 90-degree row should be read as possibly a sail-tag question rather than a model error.\n\n3. The feed publishes no heel column at all (all 284 keys of the record were enumerated; there is no heel, reef or flat field), so heelDeg is null on every row. Calibration stage 3, the heel pass, has nothing to fit against on this class and says so rather than fitting the boat to a zero.\n\n4. An ORC polar is issued per certificate, for one measured hull, not per class. ADR 0020 measured the spread across 40 Melges 24 certificates at up to 11.4 %, driven by measured displacement spanning 821-1002 kg. This is HAIZEA, POR-210, ESP INTL certificate 21001 issued 2026-03-30 -- not 'the Melges 24's polar', which is not a well-formed phrase.\n\nThe DW180, DW165, DW150, WL, CR and OC allowances the feed also carries are course and fixed-heading scoring allowances rather than polar rows, and are not transcribed."
}
